{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And I will give peace in the land.</b> After He mentioned the abundance of blessing and goodness and satiety, He sealed with the measure of peace. And our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted: perhaps you will say, behold there is food and drink — if there is no peace, it is nothing; therefore it says afterward, 'And I will give peace in the land,' for it is weighed against everything, as it says (Isaiah 45:7): ״עושה שלום ובורא את הכל״." "<b>And by way of the Kabbalah:</b> 'And I will give peace in the land' — Scripture promises that He will place the Foundation of the world (yesod olam) joined within the earth that is in Genesis, for through this the world is blessed. And it is like the matter that is written (Ecclesiastes 3:11): ״גם את העולם נתן בלבם״, for the heart is the earth, and this is clear, for therefore it says 'in the land' — 'in their heart,' for the all is in all when the wheel is within the wheel. And because the influx comes to the Foundation (yesod) from Netzah and Hod, which are 'taught of YHWH' (למודי ה') and which are the ones that flow into it, therefore our Rabbis of blessed memory said: 'disciples of the sages multiply peace in the world,' and they proved this from what is written (Isaiah 54:13): ״וכל בניך למודי ה' ורב שלום בניך״."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:28:37.349671058Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}